## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to extend Dijkstra's algorithm to count shortest paths while handling ties and modular arithmetic—a common pattern in competitive programming and graph algorithms.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm with path counting augmentation
- Non-negative edge weights, including zero-weight edges
- Modular arithmetic for large path counts and overflow prevention
- Edge case handling: unreachable destinations, multiple optimal paths, zero-weight cycles

## Code Example
```javascript
function countShortestPaths(n, edges, s, t) {
  const MOD = 1e9 + 7;
  const dist = new Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const ways = new Array(n).fill(0);

  dist[s] = 0;
  ways[s] = 1;

  const pq = new MinPriorityQueue({ priority: x => dist[x] });
  pq.enqueue(s);

  while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
    const u = pq.dequeue().element;

    for (const [v, w] of edges[u]) {
      if (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {
        dist[v] = dist[u] + w;
        ways[v] = ways[u];
        pq.enqueue(v);
      } else if (dist[u] + w === dist[v]) {
        ways[v] = (ways[v] + ways[u]) % MOD;
      }
    }
  }

  return { distance: dist[t] === Infinity ? -1 : dist[t], paths: ways[t] };
}
```

## Time & Space Complexity
- **Time**: O((N + M) log N) due to priority queue operations
- **Space**: O(N) for distance and path count arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design streaming state with sliding windows, using hash maps, per-id deques (linked lists), and a heap for ranking. Emphasizes correctness under out-of-order arrivals and lazy expirations.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding-window maintenance per key using a deque
- Lazy expiration and lazy heap invalidation
- Top-K extraction via a max-heap with versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
class RealTimeTopKWindow {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.byId = new Map(); // id -> { deque: [], sum, version }
    this.globalMax = new MinHeap((a,b)=>b.sum-a.sum); // max-heap emulation
  }
  addEvent(id, value, ts) {
    // Ensure id exists
    const rec = this.byId.get(id) || { deque: [], sum: 0, version: 0 };
    // expire old
    while (rec.deque.length && rec.deque[0].ts <= ts - this.W) {
      const old = rec.deque.shift();
      rec.sum -= old.value;
    }
    rec.deque.push({ ts, value });
    rec.sum += value;
    rec.version++;
    this.byId.set(id, rec);
    this.globalMax.push({ sum: rec.sum, id, ver: rec.version });
  }
  getTopK(K) {
    const res = [];
    const seen = new Set();
    while (res.length < K) {
      const top = this.globalMax.pop();
      if (!top) break;
      const cur = this.byId.get(top.id);
      if (!cur || cur.version !== top.ver || top.sum !== cur.sum) continue; // stale
      if (!seen.has(top.id)) {
        res.push(top.id);
        seen.add(top.id);
      }
    }
    return res;
  }
}
```

